  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.4.3: Eviction-lifecycle logging. Cache entries now emit a Debug log when they expire naturally (\"Cache entry expired: {CacheKey} in group {GroupName}\") and an Information log when evicted under memory pressure (\"Cache entry evicted under memory pressure: ...\"). Caller-initiated removals (Cache.Remove / RemoveGroup) are still logged upstream and intentionally suppressed at the eviction hook to avoid duplicate messages. This closes the lifecycle-visibility gap for persistent-cache consumers who need to audit whether their TTLs actually trigger. 100% backward compatible; opt-in via your existing LogLevel configuration (no new APIs).\n\nv1.4.2: Release notes metadata fix; same code as v1.4.1.\n\nv1.4.1: Critical fix for a deadlock introduced in 1.4.0. Synchronous Cache.Get called with a Task-returning populate (`await Cache.Get(..., async () => ...)`) could hang under single-threaded SynchronizationContexts (Blazor Server, WPF, WinForms) because the new eager size-estimator walked Task<T>.Result via JsonSerializer. Both RecomputeEstimatedSize and EstimateObjectSize now short-circuit when the value is a Task. Added a one-time Warning diagnostic (deduped per call site) that points sync-over-async callers at Cache.GetAsync. 100% backward compatible; recommended upgrade for all 1.4.0 users.",
